subagent change_risk_advisor:
    label: "Change Risk Advisor"
    description: "Assesses the risk of renaming, deleting, or changing an Opportunity field or rule, lists what depends on it, and checks real usage evidence before advising."
    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | To answer this, use the Query Records action to search the Opportunity Metadata object (Opportunity_Metadata__c) across all categories, matching the field or rule name the user mentions. Read the Related Items field for dependencies before answering. Do not use Answer Questions with Knowledge for this.
            | When the question involves whether a field or a specific value is actually used, or how often, call Get Opportunity Field Insights with the field API name (and the value in targetValue if the user named one). This queries live Opportunity records and returns real counts.
            | If Get Opportunity Field Insights returns a populatedCount or matchingValueCount of 0, state that usage is "confirmed unused" or "confirmed no records use this value" and cite the totalRecords count it checked against. Do not say "potentially unused" when this action has already confirmed zero usage.
            | If Get Opportunity Field Insights returns a count greater than 0, cite the exact numbers (for example, "142 of 4,830 Opportunities, 2.9%, have this field populated") rather than describing usage vaguely.
            | Never say a change is safe. Always identify dependencies first: validation rules, record types, business processes, CPQ (SBQQ__) fields, integration keys (External ID fields), and roll-up summary sources.
            | List every dependency you can confirm from the Opportunity_Metadata__c records before giving any guidance.
            | If dependency coverage may be incomplete, say so and tell the user to confirm with an admin or architect before proceeding.
            | End every answer with a short checklist titled "Before you proceed, check:".
        actions:
            GetOpportunityFieldInsights: @actions.GetOpportunityFieldInsights
                with fieldApiName = ...
                with targetValue = ...
            AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge: @actions.AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge
                with query = ...
                with citationsUrl = ...
                with ragFeatureConfigId = ...
                with citationsEnabled = ...
            IdentifyRecordByName: @actions.IdentifyRecordByName
                with recordName = ...
                with objectApiName = ...
            QueryRecords: @actions.QueryRecords
                with query = ...
                with customizationInstructions = ...
            GetRecordDetails: @actions.GetRecordDetails
                with recordId = ...
    actions:
        GetOpportunityFieldInsights:
            description: |
                Retrieves live field metadata, record counts, and actual usage percentages across all Opportunity records in the org for a specified field API name. Use this whenever the user asks if a field or a specific value is actually used, how many records have it populated, or wants evidence before a risky change.
            label: "Get Opportunity Field Insights"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Analyzing Opportunity field usage"
            target: "apex://OpportunityFieldInsightsAction"

            inputs:
                "fieldApiName": string
                    description: "API Name of the Opportunity field to evaluate (e.g., StageName, Custom_Field__c)."
                    label: "Field API Name"
                    is_required: True
                    is_user_input: True
                "targetValue": string
                    description: "Optional specific value to calculate usage against (e.g., Closed Won)."
                    label: "Target Value"
                    is_required: False
                    is_user_input: True

            outputs:
                "fieldLabel": string
                    description: "Label of the field, or an explanation if the field could not be found."
                    label: "Field Label"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "dataType": string
                    description: "Data type of the field."
                    label: "Data Type"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "totalRecords": integer
                    description: "Total Opportunity count in the org that the running user can see."
                    label: "Total Records"
                    is_displayable: True
                    filter_from_agent: False
                "populatedCount": integer
